Eventually, she moved to New York.
后来，她搬到了纽约。

340
00:12:50.700 --> 00:12:52.280
She studied at the actor's studio.
她在演员工作室学习。

341
00:12:52.280 --> 00:12:54.260
That's a big deal, acting school, guys.
那是很了不起的表演学校，伙计们。

342
00:12:54.920 --> 00:13:00.520
Then she made her Broadway debut in 1948 in a production called Sundown Beach.
然后她于1948年在百老汇首次登台，出演了一部名为《日落海滩》的作品。

343
00:13:00.520 --> 00:13:07.460
She became a household name when she was cast as Phyllis Lindstrom on The Mary Tyler Moore Show.
当她在《玛丽·泰勒·摩尔秀》中饰演菲莉丝·林德斯特伦时，她成了家喻户晓的名字。

344
00:13:07.780 --> 00:13:10.600
And then she had her own spinoff show, Phyllis.
之后她有了自己的衍生剧《菲莉丝》。

345
00:13:10.940 --> 00:13:16.520
She won a Best Supporting Oscar for Peter Bogdanovich's The Last Picture Show, Angela.
她凭借彼得·博格达诺维奇的《最后一场电影》赢得了奥斯卡最佳女配角奖，安吉拉。

346
00:13:16.520 --> 00:13:21.840
Which was written by Larry McMurtry, who is from my hometown of Archer City, Texas.
该片由拉里·麦克默特里编剧，他来自我的家乡德克萨斯州阿彻城。

347
00:13:21.840 --> 00:13:24.220
And they filmed it in Archer City.
而且他们就是在阿彻城拍摄的。

348
00:13:24.540 --> 00:13:29.780
And it was written by, you know, Larry never officially claimed it, but folks in Archer City.
并且它是……你知道的，拉里从未正式承认过，但阿彻城的人们……

349
00:13:29.900 --> 00:13:31.720
So they'd be like, were you so-and-so?
所以他们会问，你是某某某吗？

350
00:13:31.960 --> 00:13:33.180
Did you sleep with that person?
你跟那个人睡过觉吗？

351
00:13:33.300 --> 00:13:33.780
What's happening?
怎么回事？

352
00:13:34.300 --> 00:13:37.800
Oh, so people were like trying to figure out who everybody was.
哦，所以大家都在试图弄清楚每个人到底是谁。

353
00:13:37.940 --> 00:13:38.560
Yeah, yeah.
对，对。

354
00:13:38.580 --> 00:13:40.120
Which person is Sybil Shepard?
哪个是西碧尔·谢泼德？

355
00:13:40.260 --> 00:13:41.760
Which person is Cloris Leachman?
哪个是克洛里斯·里奇曼？

356
00:13:41.840 --> 00:13:42.620
Yeah, exactly.
对，没错。

357
00:13:42.920 --> 00:13:45.400
And Larry said it was inspired by, you know.
然后拉里说这受了启发，你知道的。

358
00:13:45.980 --> 00:13:46.280
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

359
00:13:46.440 --> 00:13:46.780
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

360
00:13:46.880 --> 00:13:47.500
I don't know.
我不知道。

361
00:13:47.580 --> 00:13:49.980
I feel like there's some woman named Doris who knows.
我觉得有个叫多丽丝的女人知道。

362
00:13:51.080 --> 00:13:52.280
She's like, it was me.
她就像是在说，就是我。

363
00:13:53.160 --> 00:13:59.620
Jenna, I actually read The Last Picture Show a few years after I had left Archer City and I was in college.
珍娜，其实我离开阿彻城几年后上大学时读了《最后一场电影》。

364
00:13:59.620 --> 00:14:00.580
I was like, you know what?
当时我想，你知道吗？

365
00:14:00.700 --> 00:14:01.940
This is a book about my hometown.
这是一本关于我老家的书。

366
00:14:01.940 --> 00:14:02.640
I want to read it.
我想读读。

367
00:14:02.740 --> 00:14:03.600
It's so great.
太棒了。

368
00:14:03.780 --> 00:14:04.600
It's a great read.
非常值得一读。

369
00:14:04.820 --> 00:14:07.220
It's a great book and a great movie is what you're saying.
你的意思是这是一本好书，也是一部好电影。

370
00:14:07.340 --> 00:14:07.500
Yeah.
对。

371
00:14:07.760 --> 00:14:10.040
So I'm saying don't skip the book on this one, guys.
所以我想说大家这次千万别错过这本书。

372
00:14:10.360 --> 00:14:17.700
Over the course of her career, she won a total of eight Emmys for both drama and comedy, by the way.
顺便说一句，在她的职业生涯中，她总共赢得了八座艾美奖，涵盖剧情类和喜剧类。

373
00:14:18.160 --> 00:14:20.060
She won a Daytime Emmy.
她赢得过日间艾美奖。

374
00:14:20.500 --> 00:14:21.880
She won a Golden Globe Award.
她赢得过金球奖。

375
00:14:22.500 --> 00:14:30.760
And in 2008, at the age of 82, she was a contestant on season seven of Dancing with the Stars.
在2008年，82岁的她成为了《与星共舞》第七季的参赛选手。

376
00:14:30.760 --> 00:14:35.160
She was the oldest contestant to ever dance on Dancing with the Stars.
她是《与星共舞》历史上年龄最大的参赛选手。

377
00:14:35.760 --> 00:14:41.320
And she was inducted into the Television Academy Hall of Fame in 2011.
她于2011年入选电视艺术与科学学院名人堂。

378
00:14:42.660 --> 00:14:45.280
I mean, the legacy of this woman.
我是说，这位女性的传奇经历。

379
00:14:45.280 --> 00:14:50.580
Sadly, she passed away in 2021 at the age of 94.
遗憾的是，她于2021年去世，享年94岁。

380
00:14:51.580 --> 00:14:54.080
And she was on our show.
而且她还上过我们的节目。

381
00:14:54.280 --> 00:14:54.900
I know.
我知道。

382
00:14:55.320 --> 00:14:56.120
This legend.
这位传奇人物。

383
00:14:56.380 --> 00:14:56.780
Legend.
传奇。

384
00:14:57.100 --> 00:14:57.940
Amazing woman.
了不起的女性。

385
00:14:58.700 --> 00:15:01.160
Jenna, did you know I got to spend a little bit of time with Cloris?
珍娜，你知道我有幸和克洛里斯相处过一段时间吗？

386
00:15:01.660 --> 00:15:02.100
Yes.
知道。

387
00:15:02.280 --> 00:15:03.520
Now, not during this episode.
当然，不是在这集拍摄期间。

388
00:15:03.740 --> 00:15:04.760
Not during this episode.
不是在这集拍摄期间。

389
00:15:04.760 --> 00:15:06.980
Because none of us met these guys during this episode.
因为我们谁都没在这集拍摄时遇到他们。

390
00:15:07.140 --> 00:15:09.440
No, we didn't film when they were there, which was a bummer.
对，他们在那的时候我们没拍，太遗憾了。

391
00:15:09.840 --> 00:15:16.580
But I ended up co-presenting an award at the 2012 Genesis Awards with Cloris.
但我后来和克洛里斯一起在2012年创世纪奖上共同颁发了一个奖项。

392
00:15:16.820 --> 00:15:18.220
We were co-presenters.
我们是联合颁奖嘉宾。

393
00:15:18.540 --> 00:15:19.180
Oh, my gosh.
哦，天哪。

394
00:15:19.240 --> 00:15:20.240
We had to hang out backstage.
我们得在后台待在一起。

395
00:15:20.240 --> 00:15:22.780
I met her daughter, Dinah, who is lovely.
我见到了她的女儿黛娜，人非常好。

396
00:15:23.300 --> 00:15:25.120
They were the cutest mother-daughter duo.
她们是最可爱的母女组合。

397
00:15:25.460 --> 00:15:27.800
And then Cloris and I went out on stage together.
然后克洛里斯和我一起走上了舞台。

398
00:15:27.800 --> 00:15:29.340
We presented this award.
我们颁了这个奖。

399
00:15:29.820 --> 00:15:32.200
And she truly was such a hoot.
她真的是个超级有趣的人。

400
00:15:33.360 --> 00:15:39.040
She, I think, was at the age in her life and in her career where she gave, as the kids say, zero Fs.
我觉得在她人生的那个阶段和职业生涯的那个时期，正如年轻人所说，她真的是毫不在乎、随心所欲。

401
00:15:39.100 --> 00:15:39.360
Uh-huh.
嗯哼。

402
00:15:40.300 --> 00:15:43.640
And then I would run into her and her daughter at different events.
然后我会在不同的活动上偶遇她和她的女儿。

403
00:15:43.640 --> 00:15:46.860
And we would say hi because we had formed this little connection.
我们会打招呼，因为我们之间建立了一种小小的联系。

404
00:15:47.280 --> 00:15:47.420
Yeah.
对。

405
00:15:47.620 --> 00:15:50.940
But anyway, she was just so fun and so full of life.
但不管怎样，她真的非常有趣，而且充满了活力。

406
00:15:50.940 --> 00:15:54.800
And I'm so glad I just got to just interact with her those few times.
我很高兴能有那几次机会和她互动。

407
00:15:55.080 --> 00:15:55.300
Yeah.
是啊。

408
00:15:55.400 --> 00:15:56.980
I love that story, Ange.
安琪，我很喜欢这个故事。

409
00:15:56.980 --> 00:16:00.140
Why don't we take a break and we'll come back and break down this episode.
我们先休息一下，回来后再剖析这一集。

410
00:16:00.520 --> 00:16:00.960
Okay, great.
好的，太棒了。

411
00:16:10.950 --> 00:16:13.970
We start this episode with Pam being kind of upset.
这一集开始时，帕姆有点难过。

412
00:16:14.170 --> 00:16:15.790
She's just gotten off the phone with her mom.
她刚跟妈妈通完电话。

413
00:16:16.250 --> 00:16:20.250
And she's going to go find Jim and say, hey, what did you say to my dad?
然后她去找吉姆，说，嘿，你跟我爸说什么了？

414
00:16:20.870 --> 00:16:21.350
Yeah.
对。

415
00:16:21.610 --> 00:16:24.670
Her idea of having Jim talk to her dad did not go well.
她让吉姆去跟她爸谈谈的想法结果并不好。

416
00:16:25.010 --> 00:16:27.670
Apparently, her dad is now looking for an apartment.
显然，她爸现在正在找公寓。

417
00:16:28.130 --> 00:16:30.450
And the divorce is on.
而且这婚是离定了。

418
00:16:30.630 --> 00:16:31.150
It's happening.
真的要离了。

419
00:16:31.590 --> 00:16:33.030
Pam gets really worried.
帕姆变得非常担心。

420
00:16:33.030 --> 00:16:38.350
She has this talking head where she says, what could Jim have said to make my dad want
她有一个单人访谈镜头，在里面她说，吉姆到底说了什么，才让我爸想要

421
00:16:38.350 --> 00:16:39.190
to leave my mom?
离开我妈？

422
00:16:39.650 --> 00:16:43.430
And at what point in their marriage is Jim going to say this to her?
而且在他们婚姻的哪个阶段，吉姆也会对她说这话？

423
00:16:43.890 --> 00:16:44.790
She's spiraling.
她情绪失控了。

424
00:16:45.010 --> 00:16:46.110
I think she's spiraling.
我觉得她快崩溃了。

425
00:16:46.190 --> 00:16:46.290
Yeah.
对。

426
00:16:46.390 --> 00:16:47.310
I mean, that's a big leap.
我是说，这跨度太大了。

427
00:16:47.450 --> 00:16:48.350
That's a big jump.
这跳跃太大了。

428
00:16:48.470 --> 00:16:49.350
But she's upset.
但她很难过。

429
00:16:49.570 --> 00:16:50.750
And she's scared.
而且她很害怕。

430
00:16:51.150 --> 00:16:51.490
Right?
对吧？

431
00:16:51.490 --> 00:16:54.050
We had a fan question from Sally Kay.
我们收到了来自莎莉·凯的一个粉丝提问。

432
00:16:54.590 --> 00:16:59.430
Was the divorce of Jim's parents a setup for the Michael-Helene relationship in season
吉姆父母的离婚是为了给第六季中迈克尔和海伦的

433
00:16:59.430 --> 00:17:00.010
six?
关系做铺垫吗？

434
00:17:00.550 --> 00:17:02.570
Helene is Pam's mom, everyone.
各位，海伦是帕姆的妈妈。

435
00:17:03.050 --> 00:17:03.610
No.
不是。

436
00:17:04.430 --> 00:17:12.370
This was crafted as a small representation of how our show had dramatic moments in addition
这个情节的设定是为了小幅度地展现我们的剧集除了喜剧效果

437
00:17:12.370 --> 00:17:13.430
to comedic ones.
之外，也有戏剧性的时刻。

438
00:17:13.430 --> 00:17:19.190
But because this aired after the Super Bowl, we wanted to stay away from existing storylines.
但因为这一集是在超级碗之后播出的，我们不想触碰现有的故事情节。

439
00:17:19.190 --> 00:17:25.410
So the writers had to create kind of like a brand new drama, but one that wouldn't go
所以编剧们不得不创造一种全新的戏剧冲突，但又不能

440
00:17:25.410 --> 00:17:28.970
on to affect our regular characters too directly.
对我们的常规角色产生太直接的影响。

441
00:17:29.190 --> 00:17:33.390
We didn't want anything in this episode to actually affect the character arcs and relationships
我们不希望这一集中的任何内容真正影响到那些已经

442
00:17:33.390 --> 00:17:34.590
that were set in place.
设定好的角色弧光和人物关系。

443
00:17:34.750 --> 00:17:35.070
Yes.
是的。

444
00:17:35.590 --> 00:17:38.750
So that was kind of why this storyline was crafted.
所以这就是设计这个故事情节的原因。

445
00:17:39.230 --> 00:17:44.890
And I remember John and I really fighting for the drama of this.
我记得我和约翰真的很为这场戏的戏剧性据理力争。

446
00:17:45.070 --> 00:17:48.430
Like really saying, no, we want to play this real.
就像是坚决要求说，不，我们要把这当作现实来演。

447
00:17:48.650 --> 00:17:50.030
Pam is really upset.
帕姆是真的很难过。

448
00:17:50.270 --> 00:17:51.970
This isn't funny upset.
这不是那种搞笑的难过。

449
00:17:52.570 --> 00:17:58.950
Like I remember when I was shooting a three-camera show, I was supposed to get mad at one of the
就像我记得以前拍三机位情景喜剧时，我本该对另一个

450
00:17:58.950 --> 00:17:59.650
other characters.
角色生气的。

451
00:17:59.690 --> 00:18:01.110
And I was supposed to call him a jerk.
而且我本来应该叫他混蛋的。

452
00:18:01.230 --> 00:18:02.390
I was supposed to say, you're a jerk.
我本该说，你这个混蛋。

453
00:18:02.390 --> 00:18:06.770
And the director came over to me and he said, I'm so sorry.
然后导演走过来跟我说，我真的很抱歉。

454
00:18:06.890 --> 00:18:08.250
This is three-camera.
这是三机拍摄。

455
00:18:09.370 --> 00:18:13.110
You need to do funny mad, not actual mad.
你需要表现得搞笑地生气，而不是真生气。

456
00:18:13.210 --> 00:18:14.910
You're doing single-camera mad.
你演的是单机拍摄的生气方式。

457
00:18:15.010 --> 00:18:15.190
Yeah.
对。

458
00:18:15.530 --> 00:18:16.890
Funny mad, funny sad.
搞笑地生气，搞笑地伤心。

459
00:18:17.250 --> 00:18:19.030
He said, maybe go up at the end.
他说，也许最后情绪可以高亢一点。

460
00:18:19.110 --> 00:18:19.990
You're a jerk.
你这个混蛋。

461
00:18:20.630 --> 00:18:21.030
Yeah.
对。

462
00:18:21.270 --> 00:18:22.410
And I was like, oh, okay.
然后我就想，哦，好吧。

463
00:18:22.630 --> 00:18:23.650
Or stomp your foot.
或者跺跺脚。

464
00:18:23.770 --> 00:18:24.410
Yeah, something.
对，随便什么。

465
00:18:24.610 --> 00:18:27.750
Drop something on your toe and then go, ow, you're a jerk.
把什么东西砸到脚趾上，然后喊，哎哟，你这个混蛋。

466
00:18:28.050 --> 00:18:28.450
Ow.
哎哟。

467
00:18:28.810 --> 00:18:31.650
Oh, see, this is why you were good at the three-camera, Angela.
哦，你看，这就是为什么你擅长三机拍摄，安吉拉。

468
00:18:32.850 --> 00:18:34.070
I couldn't get it.
我当时就是抓不住要领。

469
00:18:34.250 --> 00:18:35.010
I couldn't get it.
我当时就是抓不住。

470
00:18:35.830 --> 00:18:40.390
So anyway, John and I were like, we're going to do real upset.
所以不管怎样，我和约翰当时就觉得，我们要表现得真正心烦意乱。

471
00:18:40.790 --> 00:18:45.550
And it's going to be okay because all the rest of the episode is going to have the comedy.
而且没关系的，因为整集剩下的部分都会有喜剧效果。

472
00:18:46.770 --> 00:18:52.810
You know, the first three-camera I did after The Office, I played it really real and really
你知道的，我在《办公室》之后拍的第一部三机情景喜剧，我演得非常真实，非常

473
00:18:52.810 --> 00:18:53.210
quiet.
安静。

474
00:18:53.430 --> 00:18:55.210
It was a show called Hot in Cleveland.
那是一部叫《克利夫兰热辣惹火》的剧。

475
00:18:55.470 --> 00:18:56.870
I was really excited to do it.
我当时真的很兴奋能参演。

476
00:18:57.050 --> 00:18:58.630
Amazing actresses on that show.
那部剧里有非常棒的女演员们。

477
00:18:59.050 --> 00:19:00.630
Craig Ferguson was a guest star.
克雷格·弗格森是客串明星。

478
00:19:00.630 --> 00:19:06.290
He was in there and the director came over to me and was like, could you talk faster,
他在那里，导演走过来对我说，你能说快一点吗，

479
00:19:06.470 --> 00:19:07.230
maybe louder?
也许声音大一点？

480
00:19:07.550 --> 00:19:09.410
And could you lower your voice or something?
还有你能把声音放低点或者怎么样吗？

481
00:19:09.410 --> 00:19:10.210
I don't know.
我不知道。

482
00:19:10.490 --> 00:19:12.970
Can we get her like some glasses?
我们能给她弄副眼镜什么的吗？

483
00:19:13.950 --> 00:19:16.710
Anything to make you like a character or something.
任何能让你看起来像个角色的东西。

484
00:19:17.090 --> 00:19:17.530
Comedic.
有喜剧效果的。

485
00:19:17.670 --> 00:19:17.850
Yeah.
对。

486
00:19:18.390 --> 00:19:22.070
And Craig Ferguson started cracking up when the director walked away and he was like,
等导演走开后，克雷格·弗格森开始大笑，他说，

487
00:19:22.270 --> 00:19:25.490
maybe get her a top hat, a patch, maybe a parrot for her shoulder.
也许给她弄顶大礼帽、一个眼罩，肩膀上再弄只鹦鹉。

488
00:19:27.430 --> 00:19:32.270
And Wendy Malick was also in the scene and she came over and said to me, and she called
温迪·马利克当时也在那个场景里，她走过来对我说，她还叫

489
00:19:32.270 --> 00:19:33.530
me kid, which I loved.
我孩子，这我可太喜欢了。

490
00:19:34.050 --> 00:19:36.350
She goes, kid, you got to sell it to the back row.
她说，孩子，你得让最后一排的人也看到你的表演。

491
00:19:37.050 --> 00:19:38.230
This is multicam.
这是多机位。

492
00:19:38.590 --> 00:19:40.190
I said, gotcha, got it, got it.
我说，懂了，明白了，明白了。

493
00:19:40.330 --> 00:19:40.530
Okay.
好的。

494
00:19:40.950 --> 00:19:41.210
Yeah.
对。

495
00:19:41.810 --> 00:19:43.330
They did get me glasses though.
不过他们确实给我弄了眼镜。

496
00:19:44.170 --> 00:19:44.870
They did?
是吗？

497
00:19:45.270 --> 00:19:46.230
Were they funny?
它们滑稽吗？

498
00:19:46.710 --> 00:19:47.110
Funny.
滑稽。

499
00:19:48.330 --> 00:19:50.170
Betty White did tell me I was funny though.
不过贝蒂·怀特确实跟我说我很搞笑。

500
00:19:50.450 --> 00:19:51.270
That was my takeaway.
这就是我的收获。

501
00:19:51.690 --> 00:19:53.950
Do you have any more stories about legends?
你们还有更多关于传奇人物的故事吗？

502
00:19:53.950 --> 00:19:56.110
You've got Cloris Leachman, you've got Betty White.
有克劳丽丝·利奇曼，还有贝蒂·怀特。

503
00:19:56.150 --> 00:19:57.770
We met Carol Burnett once.
我们曾经遇到过卡罗尔·伯内特。

504
00:19:57.990 --> 00:19:59.370
Well, I didn't speak though.
不过，我当时没说话。

505
00:19:59.530 --> 00:20:00.590
Remember, I was too nervous.
记住，我太紧张了。

506
00:20:00.890 --> 00:20:02.910
I didn't speak either, but we stood next to her.
我也没有说话，但我们就站在她旁边。

507
00:20:02.930 --> 00:20:05.590
I know, but Kate Flannery talked to her and we just stood there and smiled.
我知道，但凯特·弗兰纳里和她说话了，而我们只是站在那里微笑。

508
00:20:05.750 --> 00:20:08.290
And then her and Kate got like a whole friendship going.
然后她和凯特好像就发展成了一段真正的友谊。

509
00:20:08.950 --> 00:20:13.950
We were so, we just need to go up to Carol Burnett laughing next time.
我们太……我们下次只需要笑着走到卡罗尔·伯内特面前就行了。

510
00:20:14.290 --> 00:20:15.090
Oh no.
哦，不。

511
00:20:15.730 --> 00:20:16.870
I'm going to try that one again.
我打算再试一次那个。

512
00:20:17.110 --> 00:20:19.410
I'm going to get that one out in the future.
以后我还要把那招拿出来用。

513
00:20:19.730 --> 00:20:20.710
You're going to bust it out.
你打算把它使出来。

514
00:20:20.710 --> 00:20:21.370
I am.
是的。

515
00:20:21.550 --> 00:20:21.930
All right.
好吧。

516
00:20:22.070 --> 00:20:22.790
Where are we?
我们讲到哪了？

517
00:20:22.970 --> 00:20:23.090
Okay.
好的。

518
00:20:23.310 --> 00:20:24.910
Jim and Pam are playing Real Moments.
吉姆和帕姆在玩“真实时刻”游戏。

519
00:20:25.290 --> 00:20:27.730
Michael and Dwight are sharing a bottle of mini booze.
迈克尔和德怀特在分一小瓶迷你酒。

520
00:20:27.890 --> 00:20:28.890
Very tiny bottle.
非常小的瓶子。

521
00:20:29.610 --> 00:20:33.210
Jenna, this is not the first time the tiny bottle of booze has been in an episode.
珍娜，这并不是这种迷你酒瓶第一次出现在剧集里。

522
00:20:33.450 --> 00:20:34.590
When was the first time?
第一次是什么时候？

523
00:20:34.770 --> 00:20:35.150
All right.
好吧。

524
00:20:35.250 --> 00:20:40.290
In the deleted scenes of the duel, Michael is building up the courage to tell Andy and
在《决斗》的删减片段中，迈克尔正在鼓起勇气告诉安迪，

525
00:20:40.290 --> 00:20:44.310
they're walking out to the car together and Michael hands him a mini bottle of booze
他们一起走向汽车，迈克尔在电梯里

526
00:20:44.310 --> 00:20:47.150
out of his pocket in the elevator and goes, drink this.
从口袋里掏出一个迷你酒瓶递给他，说：把这个喝了。

527
00:20:47.670 --> 00:20:49.330
And then Andy's like, I don't know.
然后安迪说，我不知道。

528
00:20:49.330 --> 00:20:50.170
I really like that.
我真的很喜欢那个。

529
00:20:50.270 --> 00:20:50.810
Okay, fine.
好吧，行。

530
00:20:50.950 --> 00:20:53.850
And he drinks it and he's like, and he's like, Angela's sleeping with Dwight.
然后他喝了，然后他说，安吉拉和德怀特在睡觉。

531
00:20:55.590 --> 00:20:58.090
So I think they have these little mini bottle of booze.
所以我认为他们有这些小型的迷你酒瓶。

532
00:20:58.230 --> 00:21:02.310
You don't start seeing them in deleted scenes till after they go to Canada.
直到他们去过加拿大之后，你才开始在删减片段里看到它们。

533
00:21:02.310 --> 00:21:06.330
And I wonder, I wonder if Michael took the mini bar stash.
我在想，我在想迈克尔是不是拿了迷你酒吧的存货。

534
00:21:06.410 --> 00:21:07.510
He 100% did.
他百分之百拿了。

535
00:21:07.630 --> 00:21:07.870
Right?
对吧？

536
00:21:08.030 --> 00:21:08.430
Of course.
当然。

537
00:21:08.670 --> 00:21:10.430
That's what I wrote in my head anyway.
反正这是我在脑子里写下的剧情。

538
00:21:10.690 --> 00:21:11.730
Or from the airplane.
或者是从飞机上拿的。

539
00:21:12.050 --> 00:21:12.450
Yes.
是的。

540
00:21:12.470 --> 00:21:13.350
From first class.
从头等舱拿的。

541
00:21:13.510 --> 00:21:13.870
Yes.
是的。

542
00:21:14.090 --> 00:21:19.330
In this scene as they're sharing this mini bottle of booze, we are reminded that Dwight
在这个场景中，当他们分享这瓶迷你酒时，我们想起了德怀特

543
00:21:19.330 --> 00:21:25.330
needs to get the signature of everyone in the office as an acknowledgement that they
需要办公室里所有人的签名，以确认他们

544
00:21:25.330 --> 00:21:30.150
have accepted his apology for dismembering the CPR dummy last week.
已经接受了他上周肢解心肺复苏模拟人的道歉。

545
00:21:30.150 --> 00:21:33.890
I mean, how many apology notes is he going to have to have people sign?
我的意思是，他到底要让大家签多少张道歉信？

546
00:21:34.030 --> 00:21:36.270
I don't know, but he has to get everyone's signature.
我不知道，但他必须得到每个人的签名。

547
00:21:36.810 --> 00:21:38.350
He's having a hard time.
他现在过得很艰难。

548
00:21:38.650 --> 00:21:40.650
That's the only thing that's stressing him out.
那是唯一让他感到压力的事情。

549
00:21:41.030 --> 00:21:43.650
Well, this is when Michael gets his big idea.
嗯，这就是迈克尔想出绝妙主意的时候。

550
00:21:44.090 --> 00:21:45.470
They should roast him.
他们应该狠狠吐槽他。

551
00:21:45.670 --> 00:21:46.030
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

552
00:21:46.670 --> 00:21:47.590
This is great.
这太棒了。

553
00:21:47.830 --> 00:21:49.890
He's going to bust into the bullpen.
他马上要冲进办公区了。

554
00:21:50.090 --> 00:21:52.870
He's going to announce, we're doing a roaSt.
他要宣布，我们要办一场吐槽大会。

555
00:21:53.010 --> 00:21:54.650
I want you to really go at me.
我希望你们待会儿狠狠地攻击我。

556
00:21:54.870 --> 00:21:55.830
Don't hold back.
别手下留情。

557
00:21:55.830 --> 00:21:59.890
Yeah, you can comment on how fit I am or the fact that I'm a womanizer.
对，你们可以评论我的身材有多好，或者我有多花心。

558
00:22:00.270 --> 00:22:03.050
He doesn't want to write the material for them, but he wants it to be good.
他自己不想写台词，但又希望效果能好一点。

559
00:22:03.850 --> 00:22:05.790
Everyone is pretty excited.
大家都很兴奋。

560
00:22:06.170 --> 00:22:10.930
I mean, Kevin is like a giggly, he's so excited.
我是说，凯文兴奋得像个咯咯笑的小女生，他太激动了。

561
00:22:12.050 --> 00:22:13.970
I liked Oscar's talking head.
我很喜欢奥斯卡的单人采访。

562
00:22:14.310 --> 00:22:14.970
Say it.
说吧。

563
00:22:15.150 --> 00:22:19.310
He was like, listen, I'm a good person, but I am going to try to make Michael cry.
他的意思是，听着，我是个好人，但我一定要把迈克弄哭。

564
00:22:21.030 --> 00:22:23.450
We had a fan catch from Samantha S.
我们收到了萨曼莎·S的粉丝发现。

565
00:22:23.670 --> 00:22:24.730
and Michelle S.
还有米歇尔·S。

566
00:22:24.850 --> 00:22:26.450
Two people noticed this catch.
有两个人发现了这个细节。

567
00:22:26.990 --> 00:22:31.810
If you're following along, starting with part two at 1 minute 15 seconds,
如果你在跟着看的话，从第二部分1分15秒开始，

568
00:22:32.290 --> 00:22:36.230
Kelly is standing in front of the shelves and her notebook is closed.
凯莉站在货架前，她的笔记本是合上的。

569
00:22:36.370 --> 00:22:40.410
But in the very next shot, it is open and upside down.
但在紧接着的下一个镜头里，本子是打开的，而且上下颠倒了。

570
00:22:40.790 --> 00:22:43.570
Oh, well, we missed that one.
哦，好吧，我们漏掉了这个。

571
00:22:43.730 --> 00:22:46.650
Clearly, she's not really taking an inventory of anything.
很显然，她根本没在盘点什么东西。

572
00:22:46.950 --> 00:22:48.270
Well, I have a question for you.
好吧，我有个问题要问你。

573
00:22:48.370 --> 00:22:48.910
What is it?
什么问题？

574
00:22:49.310 --> 00:22:50.730
Who is planning this roast?
这场吐槽大会是谁在策划？

575
00:22:51.190 --> 00:22:53.090
There's no party planning committee meeting.
根本没有开过派对策划委员会的会。

576
00:22:53.450 --> 00:22:57.170
But I want you to know, in deleted scenes, I found this gem.
但我要让你们知道，我在删减片段里发现了这个宝贝。

577
00:22:57.550 --> 00:23:00.530
Michael is having a meeting with Daryl in the warehouse.
迈克正在仓库里和达里尔开会。

578
00:23:01.190 --> 00:23:01.670
Oh.
哦。

579
00:23:01.910 --> 00:23:02.190
Yeah.
是啊。

580
00:23:02.470 --> 00:23:04.590
So I'm like, wait, is Daryl in charge of this party?
所以我当时就在想，等等，难道是达里尔在负责这个派对吗？

581
00:23:04.590 --> 00:23:05.590
Because it's in the warehouse.
因为地点在仓库。

582
00:23:06.030 --> 00:23:08.470
So Michael is telling Daryl everything he needs.
所以迈克把他的所有需求都告诉了达里尔。

583
00:23:08.550 --> 00:23:09.970
He says, I would like a stage.
他说，我想要一个舞台。

584
00:23:10.350 --> 00:23:12.630
And Daryl points to a few wood pallets.
然后达里尔指了指几块木托盘。

585
00:23:12.850 --> 00:23:13.130
Okay.
好吧。

586
00:23:13.370 --> 00:23:14.390
And he's like, well, okay.
然后他一副“好吧”的样子。

587
00:23:14.870 --> 00:23:18.110
And he goes, also, I need a big comfy chair or maybe a throne.
接着他说，还有，我需要一把大而舒服的椅子，或者一把宝座。

588
00:23:18.830 --> 00:23:20.430
That made me spit out my coffee.
这笑得我把咖啡都喷出来了。

589
00:23:20.850 --> 00:23:25.650
Then he tells Daryl that he would like all the other roasters to be up on the stage, too.
然后他告诉达里尔，他希望其他所有吐槽嘉宾也都坐在舞台上。

590
00:23:25.850 --> 00:23:29.370
Like, you know, the Comedy Central roast, where they have the dais of other roasters up there.
就像喜剧中心的吐槽大会那样，其他吐槽嘉宾都坐在主席台上。

591
00:23:29.510 --> 00:23:29.650
Yeah.
对。

592
00:23:29.650 --> 00:23:33.230
And Daryl's, like, looking at these tiny wood pallets, like, okay.
然后达里尔看着这些小木托盘，心想，好吧。

593
00:23:34.670 --> 00:23:36.670
Then Daryl's like, who's going to be in the audience?
接着达里尔问，谁会是观众？

594
00:23:37.130 --> 00:23:40.790
And Michael's like, we're going to charge $10 a head for the audience.
迈克就说，我们要向观众每人收10美元门票。

595
00:23:41.110 --> 00:23:41.550
Who's coming to this?
谁会来看这个啊？

596
00:23:41.550 --> 00:23:41.630
Yeah.
是啊。

597
00:23:41.770 --> 00:23:42.470
Who's coming to this?
谁会来看这个啊？

598
00:23:42.610 --> 00:23:44.730
Then Michael's like, oh, also, we need alcohol.
然后迈克又说，哦，还有，我们需要酒。

599
00:23:44.970 --> 00:23:45.370
Okay.
好吧。

600
00:23:45.410 --> 00:23:46.590
You need lots of alcohol.
你们需要很多酒。

601
00:23:47.210 --> 00:23:50.490
And I'm going to need something to spit in for my spit takes.
而且我还需要一个容器，用来在我喷水时吐水。

602
00:23:50.950 --> 00:23:54.930
Oh, he's planning out that this is going to be so funny.
哦，他在盘算着这个节目会有多搞笑。

603
00:23:54.930 --> 00:23:56.490
He's going to need to spit out his drink.
他打算要把喝的水喷出来。

604
00:23:56.490 --> 00:23:59.050
And Daryl's like, uh, you're not spitting in the warehouse.
然后达里尔说，呃，你可不能在仓库里乱吐。

605
00:23:59.450 --> 00:24:03.010
Then Dwight rushes in, and he's got this 8x10 photo of Michael.
接着德怀特冲了进来，手里拿着一张迈克尔的八寸乘十寸照片。

606
00:24:03.410 --> 00:24:04.930
And Michael's like, no, no, no, no, no.
而迈克尔则说，不，不，不，不，不。

607
00:24:04.970 --> 00:24:06.290
I want this photo huge.
我要把这张照片放大。

608
00:24:06.430 --> 00:24:08.170
It's got to cover, like, the whole back wall.
它得把差不多整面后墙都盖住。

609
00:24:08.290 --> 00:24:08.590
Okay?
好吗？

610
00:24:08.870 --> 00:24:09.090
Yeah.
好的。

611
00:24:09.290 --> 00:24:12.870
And then he says, I also want a drum and cymbal so I can do the ba-dum-buMs.
然后他说，我还想要一个鼓和镲，这样我就可以打出“咚咚锵”的效果。

612
00:24:12.970 --> 00:24:16.850
This is amazing because all of these things are going to appear in the warehouse.
这太绝了，因为所有这些东西后来都会出现在仓库里。

613
00:24:17.110 --> 00:24:17.410
Yes.
没错。

614
00:24:17.410 --> 00:24:21.430
So I'm thinking Daryl and Dwight planned this.
所以我认为达里尔和德怀特是幕后策划者。

615
00:24:21.610 --> 00:24:23.250
They were the PPC for this event.
他们是这次活动的派对策划委员会成员。

616
00:24:23.250 --> 00:24:28.610
I don't want to give too much of a spoiler, but next week we're going to find out what
我不想剧透太多，但下周我们就会知道

617
00:24:28.610 --> 00:24:33.390
happened to the PPC and why there is no one in charge of party planning right now.
派对策划委员会发生了什么，以及为什么现在没有人负责派对策划了。

618
00:24:33.510 --> 00:24:34.110
Oh, yeah.
哦，对。

619
00:24:34.570 --> 00:24:36.170
So this was, like, foreshadowing.
所以这就像是某种伏笔。

620
00:24:36.290 --> 00:24:36.970
A little bit.
有点像。

621
00:24:37.510 --> 00:24:40.330
Well, I guess they set everything up, and Dwight has a great idea.
好吧，我想他们把一切都布置好了，而且德怀特有个绝妙的主意。

622
00:24:40.410 --> 00:24:41.770
It's actually a great idea.
这其实是个绝妙的主意。

623
00:24:41.790 --> 00:24:42.410
It's brilliant.
太聪明了。

624
00:24:42.790 --> 00:24:47.210
He tells everyone as they're entering that they have to sign in for the roaSt.
他在每个人进场时告诉他们，必须为吐槽大会签到。

625
00:24:47.590 --> 00:24:47.970
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

626
00:24:47.970 --> 00:24:53.010
But what they're really signing is his apology acknowledgement sheet.
但他们真正签名的其实是他的道歉确认表。

627
00:24:53.230 --> 00:24:53.730
Yes.
对。

628
00:24:53.730 --> 00:24:55.150
But who catches it?
但谁看出来了？

629
00:24:55.870 --> 00:24:56.390
Phyllis.
菲利斯。

630
00:24:56.750 --> 00:24:57.650
So good.
太棒了。

631
00:24:57.870 --> 00:24:58.770
She's so good.
她太厉害了。

632
00:24:58.930 --> 00:25:01.650
She is just busting his butt through this whole episode.
她在整集里简直把迈克尔克制得死死的。

633
00:25:01.890 --> 00:25:02.790
She will not sign.
她就是不肯签字。

634
00:25:02.950 --> 00:25:03.150
Uh-uh.
呃-哈。

635
00:25:03.150 --> 00:25:04.110
She's not going to sign.
她才不会签字呢。

636
00:25:04.230 --> 00:25:05.090
She's the holdout.
她是那个死扛到底的人。

637
00:25:05.310 --> 00:25:05.490
Yeah.
对。

638
00:25:05.750 --> 00:25:07.250
Everyone takes their seats.
大家都入座了。

639
00:25:07.730 --> 00:25:09.270
Michael sits on his throne.
迈克尔坐在他的宝座上。

640
00:25:09.730 --> 00:25:12.050
And now the roast is going to begin.
现在，吐槽大会要开始了。

641
00:25:12.750 --> 00:25:13.110
Yeah.
对。

642
00:25:13.750 --> 00:25:14.490
Should we take a break?
我们要休息一下吗？

643
00:25:14.490 --> 00:25:17.370
I think we take a break, and we come back with the roasting.
我觉得我们休息一下，回来就开始吐槽。

644
00:25:28.190 --> 00:25:29.190
Okay, folks.
好了，各位。

645
00:25:29.450 --> 00:25:30.630
The roast is on.
吐槽大会开始了。

646
00:25:31.110 --> 00:25:32.970
Michael welcomes all these jerks.
迈克尔欢迎了所有这些混蛋。

647
00:25:33.310 --> 00:25:33.590
Yeah.
对。

648
00:25:33.990 --> 00:25:35.230
Who's first up?
谁是第一个？

649
00:25:35.410 --> 00:25:39.150
Who can't wait to get up there and roast Michael Scott?
谁迫不及待地想上去吐槽迈克尔·斯科特？

650
00:25:39.150 --> 00:25:42.310
He can barely finish his sentence, and she's grabbing the microphone.
他话音刚落，她就已经抢过话筒了。

651
00:25:42.550 --> 00:25:43.970
It's Angela Martin.
是安吉拉·马丁。

652
00:25:44.190 --> 00:25:44.950
That's right.
没错。

653
00:25:45.730 --> 00:25:49.930
Jenna, I noticed something in re-watching this multiple times, like we do each week.
珍娜，我在像每周一样反复观看时注意到了一点。

654
00:25:50.110 --> 00:25:54.050
Is Angela Martin ripping off Jeff Foxworthy bits?
安吉拉·马丁是在抄袭杰夫·福克斯沃西的段子吗？

655
00:25:54.630 --> 00:25:54.930
Yes.
是的。

656
00:25:55.170 --> 00:25:57.270
You know Angela Martin is a Jeff Foxworthy fan.
