00:39:21.010 --> 00:39:21.790
They thought he was kidding.
他们以为他在开玩笑。

972
00:39:21.870 --> 00:39:22.270
Yeah, yeah.
对，对。

973
00:39:22.330 --> 00:39:23.350
He said they were like, yeah, sure.
他说他们的反应是，行吧，信你才怪。

974
00:39:23.370 --> 00:39:24.010
You're going to be on.
你要上电视了。

975
00:39:24.130 --> 00:39:24.550
Yeah, whatever.
行吧，随便啦。

976
00:39:24.890 --> 00:39:26.490
And then there he was.
然后他就真的出场了。

977
00:39:26.490 --> 00:39:27.550
He was on it.
他在里面出镜了。

978
00:39:27.950 --> 00:39:31.610
Well, the episode is wrapping up and so is the movie, Mrs. Albert Hannity.
好了，这一集接近尾声，那部电影《阿尔伯特·汉尼蒂夫人》也是。

979
00:39:31.950 --> 00:39:33.310
And he's moved to tears.
他感动得热泪盈眶。

980
00:39:33.570 --> 00:39:36.790
He's watching Jack Black and Cloris Leachman break up.
他看着杰克·布莱克和克洛里斯·利奇曼分手。

981
00:39:37.190 --> 00:39:43.370
Yeah, she's very slowly moving up the staircase in her special motorized chair.
对，她坐着特制的电动椅，非常缓慢地往楼梯上挪动。

982
00:39:43.510 --> 00:39:45.290
And he's crying saying, hit reverse.
而他哭着喊道，倒车。

983
00:39:45.830 --> 00:39:51.190
So I shared last week that we shot this on location at a house in West Los Angeles.
所以我上周分享过，我们在洛杉矶西部的一处住宅实地取景拍摄的。

984
00:39:52.050 --> 00:39:56.670
Randy told me the house already had this chairlift.
兰迪告诉我，这房子本来就有这个座椅升降机。

985
00:39:56.990 --> 00:39:58.630
We did not install it.
不是我们安装的。

986
00:39:58.830 --> 00:40:02.090
I would think that they scouted a house with a chairlift.
我还以为他们是特意找了一栋带座椅升降机的房子呢。

987
00:40:02.370 --> 00:40:09.230
He also said that because they wanted this mini film to really look like a real movie,
他还说，因为他们想让这部微型电影看起来真正像一部电影，

988
00:40:09.590 --> 00:40:13.230
we shot the Mrs. Hanniday sequence on film.
我们用胶片拍摄了《汉尼蒂夫人》的片段。

989
00:40:13.490 --> 00:40:14.190
Dang.
天哪。

990
00:40:14.190 --> 00:40:18.170
It was our first time shooting something for our show on film.
这是我们节目中第一次用胶片拍摄内容。

991
00:40:18.170 --> 00:40:20.730
We normally used the digital cameras.
我们平时都用数码摄像机。

992
00:40:21.010 --> 00:40:24.830
We even had a Steadicam film camera.
我们甚至还用了一台斯坦尼康电影摄像机。

993
00:40:25.350 --> 00:40:28.690
And since they only had one day to shoot all these scenes,
而且因为他们只有一天时间来拍摄所有这些场景，

994
00:40:29.330 --> 00:40:33.650
Jeff Blitz and Randall Einhorn did a full blocking rehearsal with stand-ins
杰夫·布里茨和兰德尔·艾因霍恩带着替身进行了完整的走位排练，

995
00:40:33.650 --> 00:40:36.530
where they planned out every single shot.
他们在排练中规划了每一个镜头。

996
00:40:36.530 --> 00:40:40.450
They created official storyboards just like you do on a film.
他们制作了正式的分镜头脚本，就像拍电影时做的那样。

997
00:40:40.790 --> 00:40:42.710
And Randy even sent us pictures.
而且兰迪甚至还给我们发了照片。

998
00:40:43.110 --> 00:40:43.390
Yeah.
对。

999
00:40:43.650 --> 00:40:45.790
And they exactly match the mini movie.
而且这些照片和微型电影完全吻合。

1000
00:40:46.230 --> 00:40:48.990
There's a woman who's standing in for Cloris Leachman,
有个女替身演员在为克洛里斯·利奇曼走位，

1001
00:40:49.210 --> 00:40:51.190
kind of slowly moving up the staircase.
沿着楼梯慢慢往上走。

1002
00:40:51.370 --> 00:40:56.330
And that is how they were able to get this elaborate shoot done on film,
这就是他们能够用胶片完成这个精心拍摄的原因，

1003
00:40:56.350 --> 00:40:59.210
which normally takes a lot longer than shooting on digital.
这通常比数字拍摄需要更长的时间。

1004
00:40:59.710 --> 00:41:00.730
They could do it in one day.
他们一天就能搞定。

1005
00:41:01.050 --> 00:41:01.270
Yes.
是的。

1006
00:41:01.390 --> 00:41:03.630
So Randy sent us pictures of how they staged it.
所以兰迪给我们发了他们是如何排练的照片。

1007
00:41:03.630 --> 00:41:06.970
And it was so fun to see them because Anna, who was in charge of locations,
看到这些照片太有趣了，因为安娜，负责外景的负责人，

1008
00:41:07.450 --> 00:41:08.310
played Jack Black.
扮演了杰克·布莱克。

1009
00:41:08.570 --> 00:41:08.710
Yes.
没错。

1010
00:41:08.810 --> 00:41:11.990
And then Jasmine, who was our second AD, plays Cloris Leachman.
然后我们的第二副导演茉莉饰演克萝丽斯·利奇曼。

1011
00:41:12.150 --> 00:41:15.350
So we'll have to put one of those pictures in our stories.
所以我们得把其中一张照片发到我们的快手里。

1012
00:41:15.650 --> 00:41:16.930
It was fun to see their faces.
看到他们的脸真是有趣。

1013
00:41:17.670 --> 00:41:22.190
In addition to wrapping up the movie storyline,
除了结束电影的主线剧情，

1014
00:41:22.730 --> 00:41:27.130
we're going to find out what exactly Jim said to Pam's dad.
我们还要弄清楚吉姆究竟对帕姆的爸爸说了什么。

1015
00:41:27.470 --> 00:41:27.770
Yeah.
对。

1016
00:41:28.010 --> 00:41:31.730
Pam's dad comes to the office and they have this whole conversation in the parking lot.
帕姆的爸爸来到办公室，他们在停车场进行了整场谈话。

1017
00:41:31.890 --> 00:41:32.930
Now we can't hear it.
现在我们听不到声音。

1018
00:41:32.930 --> 00:41:34.810
We see it, but we don't know what they're saying.
我们能看到，但不知道他们在说什​​么。

1019
00:41:35.010 --> 00:41:37.170
We had a fan question from Stephanie P.
我们收到了来自斯蒂芬妮·P 的粉丝提问。

1020
00:41:37.430 --> 00:41:40.250
What did Pam say to her dad in the parking lot?
帕姆在停车场对她爸爸说了什么？

1021
00:41:40.510 --> 00:41:43.590
There was never any dialogue for this in the script.
剧本里从来没有这段对话。

1022
00:41:44.090 --> 00:41:47.010
This was always a silent spy shot.
这一直是一个无声的偷拍镜头。

1023
00:41:47.370 --> 00:41:49.230
In fact, here's what it said.
事实上，剧本上是这样写的。

1024
00:41:49.510 --> 00:41:50.270
It said,
上面写着，

1025
00:41:50.610 --> 00:41:53.910
Jim's POV, Pam is talking with her father.
吉姆的视角，帕姆正在和她的父亲谈话。

1026
00:41:54.150 --> 00:41:56.230
The conversation goes back and forth.
谈话你来我往。

1027
00:41:56.750 --> 00:41:57.750
Pam looks angry.
帕姆看起来很生气。

1028
00:41:58.130 --> 00:41:59.530
The dad says something.
爸爸说了一些话。

1029
00:41:59.910 --> 00:42:02.190
She looks up at Jim with tears in her eyes.
她眼里含着泪水抬头看着吉姆。

1030
00:42:02.190 --> 00:42:04.930
The dad leaves and Pam walks back inside.
爸爸离开了，帕姆走回里面。

1031
00:42:05.430 --> 00:42:07.890
So you guys just had to fill in the blanks there.
所以你们当时只能自己填补空白。

1032
00:42:08.050 --> 00:42:08.730
We did.
是的。

1033
00:42:09.210 --> 00:42:12.030
Now, Pam's dad was played by Rick Overton.
现在，帕姆的爸爸由里克·奥弗顿饰演。

1034
00:42:12.370 --> 00:42:14.910
And he will be back again in Niagara.
他会在《尼亚加拉》一集中再次出现。

1035
00:42:15.570 --> 00:42:17.870
And Rick is actually a really funny guy.
里克其实是个非常有趣的人。

1036
00:42:18.010 --> 00:42:20.650
He's like an improvisation comedy veteran.
他就像是一位即兴喜剧老手。

1037
00:42:21.030 --> 00:42:22.190
He's also a writer.
他也是个编剧。

1038
00:42:22.190 --> 00:42:25.330
He won an Emmy for writing an episode of Dennis Miller Live.
他因编剧一集《丹尼斯·米勒现场秀》而获得艾美奖。

1039
00:42:25.730 --> 00:42:34.890
So it's funny to me how we would cast people with great pedigree to stand and do a silent POV shot in the parking lot.
所以我觉得很有趣，我们怎么会找来背景深厚的人，只是站在停车场拍一个无声的主观镜头。

1040
00:42:34.950 --> 00:42:35.130
Yeah.
是啊。

1041
00:42:35.130 --> 00:42:38.890
But that was because this is a big role, Pam's dad.
但那是因为这是一个重要的角色，帕姆的爸爸。

1042
00:42:39.330 --> 00:42:43.810
If we bring him back, we need to make sure this person has the chops to go the distance.
如果我们让他回归，我们需要确保这个人有能力胜任长期的角色。

1043
00:42:43.950 --> 00:42:44.110
Yeah.
对。

1044
00:42:44.670 --> 00:42:45.950
And Rick was great.
里克真的很棒。

1045
00:42:46.190 --> 00:42:48.110
And we just improvised dialogue.
我们只是即兴发挥了台词。

1046
00:42:48.370 --> 00:42:54.110
We just improvised what he might be saying to her that would cause her to be hurt.
我们只是即兴发挥了他可能对她说了什么才会让她受伤。

1047
00:42:54.110 --> 00:42:59.130
It was mostly a spin on, like, I'm sorry, but I need to leave your mother, you know.
这主要围绕着，比如，我很抱歉，但我需要离开你妈妈，你知道的。

1048
00:42:59.490 --> 00:43:02.810
He knew that scripted line that Pam says later.
他知道帕姆后来要说的那些剧本台词。

1049
00:43:03.010 --> 00:43:04.490
And he would say that to me.
他会对我说那些话。

1050
00:43:04.490 --> 00:43:07.130
And I would look up at the window and all that kind of stuff.
而我会抬头看着窗户，诸如此类的事情。

1051
00:43:07.690 --> 00:43:08.370
So, yeah.
所以，是的。

1052
00:43:09.030 --> 00:43:10.090
But he was great.
但他真的很棒。

1053
00:43:10.410 --> 00:43:14.410
And by the way, he reached out to us because he knew we were coming up on this episode.
顺便说一句，他主动联系了我们，因为他知道我们快要录到这集了。

1054
00:43:14.410 --> 00:43:21.930
And he said, if you would not mind, would you tell people that I have a new improvised stand-up special called Rick Overton's Set List?
他说，如果你不介意的话，能不能告诉大家我有一个名为《里克·欧弗顿的节目单》的全新即兴单口喜剧专场？

1055
00:43:22.030 --> 00:43:24.550
And you can find it through Comedy Dynamics.
你可以通过喜剧动力公司找到它。

1056
00:43:24.750 --> 00:43:25.390
Oh, nice.
哦，不错。

1057
00:43:25.470 --> 00:43:28.490
And we can put a link in the show notes for anyone who wants to check it out.
我们可以在节目简介里放一个链接，方便任何想看的人去了解一下。

1058
00:43:28.590 --> 00:43:29.130
That's great.
那太棒了。

1059
00:43:29.390 --> 00:43:33.910
Well, this all leads us into this Pam talking head that gets quoted back to me all the time.
好了，这一切都把我们引向了帕姆的这段单人访谈，这段话总是被拿来引用。

1060
00:43:34.650 --> 00:43:36.850
It's a very sweet talking head.
这是一段非常温馨的访谈。

1061
00:43:36.910 --> 00:43:37.710
It is.
确实如此。

1062
00:43:38.230 --> 00:43:41.690
Pam says, when you're young, you assume your parents are soulmates.
帕姆说，当你年轻的时候，你以为你的父母是灵魂伴侣。

1063
00:43:42.350 --> 00:43:44.130
Her kids are going to be right about that.
她的孩子们以后也会这么觉得的。

1064
00:43:44.130 --> 00:43:44.610
Yeah.
是的。

1065
00:43:45.330 --> 00:43:48.570
Andy overhears it, throws papers in the air because he's like,
安迪无意中听到了，把文件撒向空中，因为他觉得，

1066
00:43:48.790 --> 00:43:57.610
his whole running bit is that Pam and Jim are sort of relationship geniuses and that they can see all of this stuff happening in a movie that he can't see.
他的一贯笑点就是帕姆和吉姆某种程度上是恋爱天才，他们能看出电影里发生的所有这些他看不出来的东西。

1067
00:43:57.670 --> 00:43:57.930
Yes.
没错。

1068
00:43:58.330 --> 00:44:04.330
This deep relationship-like storyline that he just can't see because it's not there, Andy.
这种深度的恋爱线索他就是看不出来，因为根本不存在，安迪。

1069
00:44:04.670 --> 00:44:05.130
No.
没错。

1070
00:44:05.350 --> 00:44:11.130
He says he would never be insightful enough to be a movie critic, but he could maybe be a food or art critic.
他说他从来没有深刻到足以当电影评论家，但他或许可以当个美食或艺术评论家。

1071
00:44:11.270 --> 00:44:11.530
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1072
00:44:12.290 --> 00:44:12.490
Hmm.
嗯。

1073
00:44:12.710 --> 00:44:12.890
Hmm.
嗯。

1074
00:44:13.370 --> 00:44:16.970
Here comes Michael in his black turtleneck and his black coat.
迈克尔穿着他的黑色高领毛衣和黑色外套进来了。

1075
00:44:17.130 --> 00:44:18.770
I'm still, like, obsessed with this outfit.
我简直对这套衣服着迷。

1076
00:44:19.270 --> 00:44:24.710
He said he spent the afternoon in the park trying to feed pigeons, but I guess they'd all flown west for the winter.
他说他整个下午都在公园里试图喂鸽子，但我想它们大概都飞到西方过冬去了吧。

1077
00:44:24.910 --> 00:44:25.110
Yeah.
是的。

1078
00:44:25.710 --> 00:44:28.450
And he just had some thoughts he wanted to share with everyone.
他只是有一些想法想和大家分享。

1079
00:44:29.810 --> 00:44:30.990
Pam says what?
帕姆说了什么？

1080
00:44:31.710 --> 00:44:32.130
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1081
00:44:32.470 --> 00:44:34.930
And he said, I wrote them down so I wouldn't forget.
他说，我都写下来了，免得忘了。

1082
00:44:35.350 --> 00:44:35.990
Oh, boy.
噢，天哪。

1083
00:44:36.270 --> 00:44:36.910
Here it comes.
来了。

1084
00:44:37.210 --> 00:44:39.910
This is the Boom Roasteds.
这就是“轰，烤得好”的桥段。

1085
00:44:40.350 --> 00:44:41.170
It is.
确实。

1086
00:44:41.290 --> 00:44:42.150
Boom Roasted.
轰，烤得好。

1087
00:44:42.150 --> 00:44:48.210
So, you know, I told you that Halstead Sullivan came up with the idea for the roast storyline.
所以呢，我告诉过你，霍尔斯特德·沙利文想出了吐槽剧情的主意。

1088
00:44:48.530 --> 00:44:48.670
Yeah.
对。

1089
00:44:48.990 --> 00:44:52.390
I had to know who came up with Boom Roasted.
我必须弄清楚是谁想出了“轰，烤得好”。

1090
00:44:52.630 --> 00:44:53.150
Who did?
是谁？

1091
00:44:53.410 --> 00:44:53.770
All right.
好吧。

1092
00:44:53.770 --> 00:44:58.150
I got a hot tip that it might be Justin Spitzer or Gene Stubnitsky.
我得到了一个内部消息，说可能是贾斯汀·斯皮策或吉恩·斯图布尼斯基。

1093
00:44:58.410 --> 00:44:58.630
Okay.
好的。

1094
00:44:58.990 --> 00:45:00.290
I reached out to them.
我联系了他们。

1095
00:45:00.610 --> 00:45:00.970
And?
然后呢？

1096
00:45:01.150 --> 00:45:01.410
Nope.
不是。

1097
00:45:01.710 --> 00:45:01.990
Nope.
不是。

1098
00:45:02.370 --> 00:45:05.450
They thought maybe it was Charlie Grandy.
他们觉得可能是查理·格兰迪。

1099
00:45:05.450 --> 00:45:06.110
Oh.
哦。

1100
00:45:06.410 --> 00:45:06.970
Was it?
是吗？

1101
00:45:07.170 --> 00:45:08.670
I don't have Charlie's info.
我没有查理的联系方式。

1102
00:45:08.930 --> 00:45:09.190
Oh.
哦。

1103
00:45:09.650 --> 00:45:11.330
So I reached out to Jen Salata.
所以我联系了詹·萨拉塔。

1104
00:45:11.570 --> 00:45:12.350
Plot thickens.
情节越来越扑朔迷离了。

1105
00:45:12.530 --> 00:45:17.250
I said, Jen, do you know if Charlie Grandy wrote Boom Roasted?
我说，詹，你知道查理·格兰迪是不是写了《烤糊了》吗？

1106
00:45:17.470 --> 00:45:17.670
Yeah.
对。

1107
00:45:18.030 --> 00:45:19.870
These are the emails I exchanged with people now.
这些是我现在跟别人通过邮件往来的内容。

1108
00:45:19.890 --> 00:45:20.050
I know.
我知道。

1109
00:45:20.210 --> 00:45:20.670
Oh, I know.
哦，我懂。

1110
00:45:21.470 --> 00:45:24.350
Jen said, I think so, but let me text him.
詹说，我记不太清，不过我发个短信问问他。

1111
00:45:24.730 --> 00:45:27.210
And then I just love Jen Salata so much.
然后我真的太喜欢詹·萨拉塔了。

1112
00:45:27.370 --> 00:45:27.890
I know.
我知道。

1113
00:45:28.070 --> 00:45:29.170
She writes me back.
她回信给我了。

1114
00:45:29.390 --> 00:45:30.990
Boom Roasted was Charlie!
《烤糊了》就是查理写的！

1115
00:45:31.250 --> 00:45:32.390
Three exclamation points.
三个感叹号。

1116
00:45:32.650 --> 00:45:33.550
We did it.
我们成功了。

1117
00:45:33.550 --> 00:45:37.050
So I wrote Justin and I said, Justin, it was Charlie Grandy.
所以我写信给贾斯汀，我说，贾斯汀，那是查理·格兰迪写的。

1118
00:45:37.150 --> 00:45:37.710
And he said, great.
他说，太好了。

1119
00:45:37.790 --> 00:45:40.910
I would like some credit on the podcast for sending you down the right road.
我希望在播客里因为指引你走上正确的道路而获得一些功劳。

1120
00:45:41.110 --> 00:45:42.050
I said, you will get it.
我说，你会得到的。

1121
00:45:42.330 --> 00:45:43.090
Thank you, Justin.
谢谢你，贾斯汀。

1122
00:45:43.450 --> 00:45:44.750
Thank you, all of you guys.
谢谢你们所有人。

1123
00:45:44.750 --> 00:45:45.290
I know.
我知道。

1124
00:45:45.450 --> 00:45:45.710
I know.
